With skills.materialize on and skills.agents not false, a start writes the shipped agents as unreagent-<name>.md into the agents/ directory next to skills.dir, and the rules file as .claude/rules/unreagent.md, only when skills.dir is <x>/.claude/skills; otherwise it writes none and logs one line. Skill names in the agent files are mapped through skillDirName. Each launcher-written file carries a content hash: absent means write; prefix and valid hash means ours and unedited, so replace or sweep; anything else is foreign or user-edited, so it is left alone and named in a WARN. A dropped agent is swept. The replace is atomic. run() is not touched beyond what setupSkills already wires.

